    {
      "id": "64c47f659333-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "What day of the week would it be on 30 th March 2020?",
      "questionHtml": "What day of the week would it be on 30<sup>th</sup> March 2020?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Sunday",
          "html": "Sunday"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Saturday",
          "html": "Saturday"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Monday",
          "html": "Monday"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Friday",
          "html": "Friday"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Here, the year is 2020 = 2000 + 19 (as 2020 is running year).</p>\n\n<p>Number of odd days in 2000 = 0</p>\n\n<p>In 19, there are 4 leap years and 15 ordinary years.</p>\n\n<p>So, no. of odd days in 4 leap year = 8 as in one leap year there are 2 odd days.</p>\n\n<p>no. of odd days in 15 ordinary years = 15, as there is 1 odd day in one year.</p>\n\n<p>no. of odd days in march = 3 + 1 = 4</p>\n\n<p>no. of odd days in date (30) = 4 weeks and 2 odd days</p>\n\n<p>Total odd days = 2 + 8 + 15 + 4 = 29 i.e. 4 weeks and 1 odd day</p>\n\n<p>And according to the days code = 1 odd day means Monday.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is Monday.</p>\n",
