      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "64c47f659333-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "If 18 th February, 2005 falls on Friday then what will be the day on 18th February, 2007?",
      "questionHtml": "If 18<sup>th</sup> February, 2005 falls on Friday then what will be the day on 18th February, 2007?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Sunday",
          "html": "Sunday"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Monday",
          "html": "Monday"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Tuesday",
          "html": "Tuesday"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Wednesday",
          "html": "Wednesday"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Concept:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">The number of days in<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> a normal year</span> is 365 i.e. <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">52 week 1 day</span> </p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, we can say every year we get <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">1 odd day</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">The number of days in <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">a leap year</span> is 366 i.e. <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">52 week 2 days</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, we can say every leap year we get <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">2 odd days</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">There has<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> no leap year</span> between 2005 and 2007.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">From 18<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2005 to 18<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2006 : <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">There has only</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> 1 odd day.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So,<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> 18</span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2006 = Friday + 1 = Saturday.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">From 18<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2006 to 18<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2007<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> </span>: <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">There has only</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> 1 odd day.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So,<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> 18</span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"><span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">th</span> February , 2007 = Saturday + 1 = Sunday.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Hence, the correct answer is<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\"> \"Sunday\"</span>.</p>\n",
