      "id": "64c47f659333-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Find the angle between the hour hand and minute hand at 5:40?",
      "questionHtml": "Find the angle between the hour hand and minute hand at 5:40?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "40&deg;",
          "html": "40&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "50&deg;",
          "html": "50&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "70&deg;",
          "html": "70&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "60&deg;",
          "html": "60&deg;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>The angle between the&nbsp;hour hand and minute hand =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(60H -11M\\over2\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>Here, H = hour M = minutes.</p>\n\n<p>Given H = 5 and minutes = 40.</p>\n\n<p>So, Angle =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((60\\times5 - 11\\times40)\\over2\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>= 70&deg;</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is&nbsp; 70&deg;.</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "64c47f659333-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "A clock is started at noon. By 20 minutes past 5, the hour hand has turned through",
      "questionHtml": "A clock is started at noon. By 20 minutes past 5, the hour hand has turned through",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "160&deg;",
          "html": "160&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "150&deg;",
          "html": "150&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "155&deg;",
          "html": "155&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "145&deg;",
          "html": "145&deg;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>The angle forms for Hour Hand:-</p>\n\n<p>12 hours =<strong> 360&deg;</strong></p>\n\n<p>1 hour = <strong>30&deg;</strong></p>\n\n<p>1 minute = <strong>0.5&deg;</strong></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the angle traced by an hour hand in 1 minute is: 0.5&deg;</p>\n\n<p><strong>The clock time moves from 12:00 (noon) to 5:20. </strong></p>\n\n<p>This duration in minute&nbsp;is 5 hours and 20 minutes =&nbsp;(5 * 60) + 20 = <strong>320 minutes.</strong></p>\n\n<p>Thus, the angle traced by an hour hand in 320 minutes is: <strong>320 &times; 0.5&deg; = 160&deg;</strong></p>\n\n<p>So, the hour hand is turned through&nbsp;160&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is <strong>&quot;</strong><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">160&deg;</span><strong>&quot;</strong><em><strong>.</strong></em></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "64c47f659333-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "If in a water image a clock shows time as 11 ∶ 35. What is the actual time in the clock?",
      "questionHtml": "If in a water image a clock shows time as 11&nbsp;∶ 35. What is the actual time in the clock?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6 ∶ 50",
          "html": "6&nbsp;∶ 50"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "6 ∶ 55",
          "html": "6&nbsp;∶ 55"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "5 ∶ 45",
          "html": "5&nbsp;∶ 45"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "7 ∶ 40",
          "html": "7&nbsp;∶ 40"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>The pattern followed here is:</p>\n\n<p>Given imaginary time in the clock in water image = 11&nbsp;∶&nbsp;35.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Using Formula:-</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Real time + Water image time = 18 ∶</strong><strong>&nbsp;30.</strong></p>\n\n<p>Real time = 18 ∶&nbsp;30 - water image time</p>\n\n<p><strong>18 </strong>∶<strong>&nbsp;30 can be considered as 17 ∶</strong><strong>&nbsp;90 (17 ∶</strong><strong>&nbsp;60 + 30) because it will simplify the subtraction process.</strong></p>\n\n<p>Real time = 17 ∶&nbsp;90 - 11&nbsp;∶&nbsp;35</p>\n\n<p>Real time = 6&nbsp;∶&nbsp;55<strong>&nbsp;(Here, decimal cycle is of 60, as 60 minutes = 1 hour).</strong></p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is<strong> &quot;6&nbsp;</strong>∶<strong>&nbsp;55&quot;.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Real time + Mirror image time = 23 ∶&nbsp;60.</li>\n\t<li>If the imaginary&nbsp;time in water image time is less than 6, then the given imaginary&nbsp;time is subtracted from 6 ∶&nbsp;30.</li>\n</ul>\n",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "64c47f659333-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "If 30 April 1983 was a Saturday, then what was the day of the week on 13 August 1989?",
      "questionHtml": "If 30 April 1983 was a Saturday, then what was the day of the week on 13 August 1989?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Thursday",
          "html": "Thursday"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Sunday",
          "html": "Sunday"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Monday",
          "html": "Monday"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Friday",
          "html": "Friday"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "No of days from 1 May 1983 to 13 August 1989 = 245 + 732 + 1095 + 225 = 2297. Since, it was Saturday on 30 April 1983, every 7th day from 30 April will be a Saturday. Thus, no. of odd days = 2297/7 = 1\n<p>→ Now, 30 April 1983 (Saturday) + 1 odd day = 13 August 1989 (Sunday)</p>\n",
